The analysis model draws on two papers. This product contains no source code
from either paper or its reference implementation.

Dongrui Liu et al., "AgentDoG: A Diagnostic Guardrail Framework for AI Agent
Safety and Security", arXiv:2601.18491v2,
https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.18491. The design borrows the 8/14/10 risk taxonomy
and the treatment of a whole agent trajectory as the unit of analysis. The
paper's reference repository (https://github.com/AI45Lab/AgentDoG) is licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0; the paper itself is distributed under
the arXiv non-exclusive distribution license.

Jiaqi Luo et al., "AgentGuard: An Attribute-Based Access Control Framework for
Tool-Use LLM-Based Agent", arXiv:2605.28071v1,
https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.28071. The design borrows the runtime attribute
vocabulary (principal, tool, arguments, target and trust) and the idea of
applying policy to single tool calls and tool chains. The paper's reference
repository (https://github.com/WhitzardAgent/AgentGuard) is licensed under
GPL-3.0, while the paper's availability section states MIT. No code from
either is included here.

See docs/agent/papers.md for the ideas adopted and left out.

